 HISTORY                                                          4002 1451
 -------                                                          4002 1451
 The inelastic thermal scattering law data for FLiBe was          4002 1451
 developed by the Low Energy Interaction Physics (LEIP) group at  4002 1451
 North Carolina State University (USA) using molecular dynamics   4002 1451
 methods [1,2]. This material is a liquid salt mixture, such that 4002 1451
 the diffusive contribution to the TSL is expected to be          4002 1451
 consequential. The FLASSH code was used with a Schofield         4002 1451
 diffusion model to produce File 7 for Be in FLiBe [3]. Please see4002 1451
 the README for additional information.                           4002 1451
                                                                  4002 1451
